<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's Democratic Party of Afghanistan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1965–1992</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as PDPA</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's Democratic Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> was a Marxist-Leninist party founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> in 1965 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-muhammad-taraki">Nur Muhammad Taraki</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babrak-karmal">Babrak Karmal</a> and others. Split into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalq">Khalq</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parcham">Parcham</a> factions, it seized power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saur-revolution">Saur Revolution</a> of April 1978 and ruled the Democratic Republic of Afghanistan with Soviet backing. Renamed the Watan Party in 1990, it lost power when the mujahideen took Kabul in 1992.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peoples-democratic-party-of-afghanistan.jpg" alt="People's Democratic Party of Afghanistan" width="320" height="327" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Falerístico · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_People%27s_Democratic_Party_of_Afghanistan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
